# `HS²` under `SO₀(1,2)`: the analytic model, its five orbits, and HS-surfaces

Target `T-bbs-hs-model` (`roadmap/roadmap.toml`; DEC-192: layer L2 lives in lean-gx; wave W0 of
`papers/bbs/REVIEW.md` §E, at `n = 2`, without the point-links and stabilisers of the L2 table).
`papers/bbs/legacy/labeled/colI_v1.tex`. 0 `sorry`.

* `bbsdef:hs_surface_topological_surface_endowed` — `colI_v1.tex:615` — partial (unmarked):
  `GX.IsHSSurface`, every word of the definition formalized; "topological surface" is read
  `GX.IsTopologicalSurface` (Hausdorff, locally homeomorphic to `ℝ²`, no countability and no
  connectedness), a reading the paper does not settle (SCOPE (c), a question).
  `GX.isHSSurface_iff`: given the `(SO₀(1,2), HS²)`-structure, only Hausdorffness is left.

> Denote by ${\operatorname{HS}}^2$ the set of geodesic rays into $\R^{1,2}$. It admits a natural
> decomposition in five subsets: the domains $\HH^2_+$ and $\HH^2_-$ comprising respectively future
> oriented and past oriented time-like rays, the domain $\dS^2$ comprising space-like rays, the two
> circles $\partial\HH^2_+$ and $\partial\HH^2_-$, boundaries of $\HH^2_\pm$ in $\HS^2$. (l.584–590)
>
> The domains $\HH^2_\pm$ are the Klein models of the hyperbolic plane, and $\dS^2$ is the Klein
> model of de Sitter space of dimension $2$. The group $\SO_0(1,2)$, \textit{i.e.} the group of of
> time-orientation preserving and orientation preserving isometries of $\R^{1,2}$, acts naturally
> (and projectively) on $\HS^2$, preserving this decomposition. (l.593–596)
>
> A HS-surface is a topological surface endowed with a $(\SO_0(1,2), \HS^2)$-structure. (l.616)

## Main declarations

* **The model.** `GX.HS d = RaySphere (Causal.Minkowski d)` (BBS-Q3's unit sphere, of the sup
  norm `max(|t|, ‖x‖)` of lean-causal's `Minkowski d`); `SO₀(1,d) = Causal.Flat.lorentz d` acts by
  the normalised action `GX.linRaySmul` (`GX.hsAction`). `HSᵈ` **is the set of rays**:
  `GX.raySphereHomeomorphRaySpace : RaySphere V ≃ₜ (V ∖ 0)/ℝ₊*`, equivariant
  (`GX.hs_homeomorph_raySpace_smul`). **Analytic**: `GX.isAnalyticAction_hs` (faithful and rigid:
  `GX.hs_eq_of_eqOn`, through `GX.eq_smul_of_eventually_eigen`), `GX.analyticStructure_hs2`.
  `HS² ≃ₜ 𝕊²` (`GX.hs2HomeomorphSph2`), charted on `ℝ²` (`GX.hs2ChartedSpace`), locally
  unloopable (`GX.isLocallyUnloopable_hs2`), locally path connected, semilocally simply connected.
* **The five orbits** (`GX.HSPiece`, `GX.HS.piece`, `GX.HS.region`): a partition
  (`GX.HS.iUnion_piece`, `GX.HS.pairwise_disjoint_piece`) preserved by `SO₀(1,d)`
  (`GX.HS.smul_mem_piece_iff`); each piece is one orbit (`GX.HS.orbit_eq_piece`, `d ≥ 2`), so
  **`HSᵈ` has exactly five orbits** (`GX.HS.orbitEquiv`, `GX.HS.card_orbitRel_quotient`);
  `ℍᵈ±`, `dSᵈ` open, `closure ℍᵈ± = ℍᵈ± ∪ ∂ℍᵈ±`, **`frontier ℍᵈ± = ∂ℍᵈ±`**
  (`GX.HS.frontier_hypPlus`, `…_hypMinus`); `ℍᵈ₊ ≃ₜ` the open unit ball (the Klein disc
  `{t = 1}`, `GX.HS.hypPlusHomeomorph`) with the projective action
  (`GX.HS.coe_smul_of_isFutureCausal`); `∂ℍᵈ₊ ≃ₜ 𝕊ᵈ⁻¹` (`GX.HS.bdPlusHomeomorph`), the action
  being lean-causal's `lorentzSphere` (`GX.HS.smul_nullPt`); `dSᵈ ≃ₜ ]−1, 1[ × 𝕊ᵈ⁻¹`.
* **The group** (BBS-Q6; DEC-152). Transitivity uses only `GX.HS.rot` (spatial `SO(d)`) and
  `GX.HS.boost` (lean-causal's `stdBoost`): `GX.HS.exists_boostRot_smul_eq`,
  `GX.HS.orbit_eq_piece_of_le` (any subgroup containing them). **Cartan decomposition**:
  `GX.HS.boostRot_eq_top`, rotations and one-axis boosts generate `lorentz d` (`d ≥ 2`).
* **HS-surfaces**: `GX.IsTopologicalSurface`, `GX.IsHSSurface`, `GX.isHSSurface_iff`;
  `HS²` is one (`GX.isHSSurface_hs2`), and so is every open subset of one (`GX.IsHSSurface.opens`).
* **A finding** (l.605–606, prose, no label): the hyperbolic clause has its counts swapped. The
  hyperbolic boost `B_ζ` fixes exactly one opposite pair in `dS²` (`GX.HS.boost_fixed_deSitter_iff`,
  `GX.HS.boost_fixed_deSitter_ncard`) and exactly two points of `∂ℍ²₊`, hence two opposite pairs
  in `∂ℍ²±` (`GX.HS.boost_fixed_bdPlus_iff`); the printed clause says one pair in `∂ℍ²±`, two in `dS²`.

## Hypothesis checklist

| BBS | here |
|---|---|
| `HS²` "the set of geodesic rays into `ℝ^{1,2}`" (l.584–585) | ✓ `HS 2`, the unit sphere of `Minkowski 2`; homeomorphic to `(ℝ^{1,2} ∖ 0)/ℝ₊*`, equivariantly (`raySphereHomeomorphRaySpace`, `hs_homeomorph_raySpace_smul`) |
| `SO₀(1,2)` "time-orientation preserving and orientation preserving isometries of `ℝ^{1,2}`" (l.594–595) | ✓ `Causal.Flat.lorentz 2`: linear, `minkQ`-preserving, future cone into itself, `det = 1` (the linear part of DEC-152's `Causal.Flat.isom 2`); generated by rotations and boosts (`boostRot_eq_top`) |
| "acts naturally (and projectively)" (l.596) | ✓ `[v] ↦ [A v]` on rays; the chart `{t = 1}` of `ℍ²₊ ∪ ∂ℍ²₊` is projective (`coe_smul_of_isFutureCausal`) |
| "preserving this decomposition" (l.596) | ✓ `smul_mem_piece_iff`; and the five pieces are exactly the orbits (`orbit_eq_piece`) |
| "the two circles `∂ℍ²±`, boundaries of `ℍ²±` in `HS²`" (l.590) | ✓ `frontier_hypPlus`, `frontier_hypMinus`, `bdPlusHomeomorph` (a circle for `d = 2`) |
| `(G, X)`-structure (l.616) | ✓ gx's: `ChartedSpace (HS 2) M`, `HasGroupoid M (gxGroupoid (lorentz 2) (HS 2))`, over the maximal atlas (DEC-16); the model is analytic (`analyticStructure_hs2`) |
| "topological surface" (l.616) | ⚠ reading (SCOPE (c)): Hausdorff and locally `ℝ²`; no countability, no connectedness |

## SCOPE (disclosed)

* **(a) The representation (BBS-Q3).** `HSᵈ` is the unit sphere of the sup norm of
  `Causal.Minkowski d`, so `ℍᵈ₊` is literally the Klein disc `{t = 1, ‖x‖ < 1}` and `∂ℍᵈ₊` is
  lean-causal's `nullVec` image. The choice of norm is immaterial (`raySphereHomeomorph`), and the
  model is the space of rays (`raySphereHomeomorphRaySpace`): no reading is left here.
* **(b) The group (BBS-Q6).** The paper defines `SO₀(1,2)` at l.594–595 as the time-orientation
  and orientation preserving isometries, which is `Causal.Flat.lorentz 2` (the isometries of
  `ℝ^{1,2}` acting on rays at `0` are the linear ones). That this group is the identity component
  of `O(1,2)` is not proved (there is no topology on `lorentz d` at this pin); it is generated by
  one-parameter subgroups (`boostRot_eq_top`), and every orbit statement holds for each subgroup
  containing the rotations and one-axis boosts (`orbit_eq_piece_of_le`).
* **(c) "Topological surface"** is read Hausdorff + locally homeomorphic to `ℝ²`
  (`IsTopologicalSurface`), the most inclusive reading: second countability (or paracompactness)
  and connectedness are not asked. A question for the author. The second field of
  `IsTopologicalSurface` is automatic for an HS-structure (`isHSSurface_iff`).
* **(d) Not formalized here** (prose of §3.1–3.2, no label): the Klein **metrics** of `ℍ²±` and
  `dS²` (only the Klein charts and the projective action are built), `SO₀(1,2) ≈ PSL(2,ℝ)`, the
  classification of elements by their fixed points (l.598–608; only the standard boost's fixed
